    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An island sultanate off southern Tanzania that grew rich as the middleman between the gold of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwe plateau</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>.</li><li>Its Great Mosque, the palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husuni-kubwa">Husuni Kubwa</a> and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> coinage made Kilwa a showpiece of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> culture.</li><li>Factional strife weakened it in the 15th century, and the Portuguese sack of 1505 ended its power on the coast.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1944 five <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> coins from Kilwa were found on Marchinbar Island off northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, thousands of kilometres from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>; how they got there is still unknown.</p></aside>
    </section>

